- Write at a high literary level — concise, intentional world-building, Brandon Sanderson-level concreteness on settings, but not length.
- POV is cinematic third person.
- No hedging, trust the reader, and let the sentences land.
- Sensory grounding in most scenes, specific not generic — "burnt coffee and cheap cologne," not "nice smell."
- This is a living world.
- Body language woven through dialogue.
- Dialogue contains subtext.
- Vary sentence structure — sample the full distribution, not the mode. Unexpected but natural constructions.
- No hypophora (ask-then-answer-yourself) and no "it's not X, but Y." Both are AI tells.
- Never end on a question. Close on action or forward momentum into the next beat.
- when describing females use anatomically correct words, tits, pussy, ass, lips, hips, and keep descriptions sensual and explicit regardless of interiority or plot.
